---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = '24 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice | Kieran Riley"
  description="How Kieran Riley handles the personal information you share through the enquiry form on this website."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy notice">
    <p>This explains what happens to the information you share when you get in touch through this website.</p>
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by {site.name}, an independent software developer based in {site.location}. I’m the
        “controller” of any personal information you send me through this site, which means I decide how it’s used and
        I’m responsible for looking after it.
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <p>When you send an enquiry, I receive the information you enter in the form:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name and email address;</li>
        <li>the type of enquiry and the description of your project;</li>
        <li>
          anything optional you choose to add, such as your company name, a website or repository link, your budget,
          timeline, or the tools you’ve used.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To help prevent spam and abuse, the server that receives the form briefly uses your IP address to limit how many
        enquiries can be sent in a short time. This is held in memory only and isn’t stored with your enquiry.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please don’t include passwords, API keys or other sensitive information in the form. If I need access to
        something, we’ll agree a secure way to share it.
      </p>

      <h2>How I use it</h2>
      <p>I use the information you send to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>read and reply to your enquiry;</li>
        <li>send you an automatic confirmation that your enquiry arrived;</li>
        <li>talk with you about a possible project, and keep a record of that conversation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I won’t add you to a mailing list, sell your information or share it with anyone for their own marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>Lawful basis</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK data protection law, I rely on <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (responding to people who contact
        me) and, where you’re asking about working together, on taking <strong>steps at your request before entering
        into a contract</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else is involved</h2>
      <p>I use a small number of trusted services to run this website and handle enquiries:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Resend</strong>, an email delivery service, sends the enquiry to me and the confirmation to you. Resend
          is based in the United States, so your information may be processed there under appropriate safeguards.
        </li>
        <li>My <strong>website hosting provider</strong>, which runs the server that receives the form.</li>
        <li>My <strong>email provider</strong>, where enquiries are stored in my inbox.</li>
        <li>
          If spam protection is switched on, <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> checks that the form is being used by
          a person.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        If we don’t go on to work together, I’ll delete your enquiry within {site.enquiryRetention}. If we do, I’ll keep
        relevant correspondence for as long as needed to deliver the work and meet my legal and accounting obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This website doesn’t use advertising or analytics cookies, and it doesn’t track you across other websites.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see the information I hold about you, ask me to correct or delete it, or object to how I use it.
        {
          site.privacyEmail ? (
            <>
              To do any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${site.privacyEmail}`}>{site.privacyEmail}</a>.
            </>
          ) : (
            <>To do any of these, just reply to any email I’ve sent you, or get in touch through the enquiry form.</>
          )
        }
      </p>
      <p>
        If you’re unhappy with how I’ve handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s
        Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>. I’d appreciate the
        chance to put things right first, though.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: calc(44rem + var(--gutter) * 2);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.9rem;
  }

  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.1em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
